From 91f39fb5469efcd217f036580654a9c39e47872b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxime <maxime.lefrancois@emse.fr>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 02:12:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Support rml:childMap and rml:parentMap in join conditions
 (RML-Core)

RML-Core allows the two sides of a join condition to be expression maps,
rml:childMap and rml:parentMap (a reference, a template or a constant), in
place of rml:child and rml:parent. Such a join condition was not read: the
referencing object map joined every child to every parent (RMLTC0030a-f,
kg-construct/rml-core).

The join condition query now reads both forms; JoinCondition keeps the type
of each side, and merge_data joins a template or a constant side on a column
of its string values. A self join is only removed when both sides are the
same reference. Test: test/join-term-maps (RMLTC0030a-c).
